# Example pathset config for MANPATH (config name: man).
#
# Copy to:
#   ~/.config/pathset/man         (canonical)
#
# Then add to your shell rc:
#   zsh/bash:  export MANPATH="$(pathset -f man -q)"
#   fish:      set -gx MANPATH (pathset -f man -q | string split :)
#
# Syntax is identical to the path config — see `pathset -h`.

# --- User-installed man pages ---------------------------------------------
?~/.local/share/man

# --- Homebrew -------------------------------------------------------------
?$HOMEBREW_PREFIX/share/man

# --- System ---------------------------------------------------------------
/usr/local/share/man
/usr/share/man
